## Part V — Measurement Framework

The transition from narrative-based education to measurable capability engineering is one of the defining structural advances of this framework. Three primary indices constitute the Martian Eco Graduate Profile.

**Multiplanetary Cognitive Index (MCI)**

The MCI measures scientific reasoning depth, systems modeling capacity, cross-disciplinary integration, and long-horizon thinking. It is assessed through structured problem-solving challenges designed to require integration across at least three of the six pillars simultaneously; systems design projects involving real complexity and genuine uncertainty; and multi-domain scenario analysis exercises evaluated by interdisciplinary panels. MCI scores are calibrated against benchmark performance across student cohorts globally, with normalization procedures accounting for educational resource inequality.

**AI Epistemic Fluency Score (AEFS)**

The AEFS measures the capacity to use AI systems productively, evaluate their outputs critically, detect bias and confabulation reliably, anchor AI-generated claims in physical or peer-validated reality, and reason ethically about AI deployment. It is assessed through AI audit exercises, epistemic integrity challenges, comparative model analysis tasks, and collaborative research projects requiring genuine human-AI epistemic partnership. The AEFS is not a measure of AI enthusiasm. It is a measure of AI sovereignty — the capacity to remain epistemically independent while working with intelligent systems.

**Psychological Stability Under Isolation Score (PSUIS)**

The PSUIS measures behavioral performance across stress tolerance, emotional regulation, conflict de-escalation, uncertainty endurance, and cooperative functioning under graduated simulation conditions. It draws on facilitated behavioral observation, peer evaluation protocols, simulation performance data, and longitudinal tracking across the student's time within the framework. Crucially, the PSUIS is not a measure of emotional suppression or artificial stoicism. It is a measure of adaptive functioning — the capacity to remain cognitively effective and relationally constructive while under genuine psychological pressure.

These three indices, combined with demonstrated ethical reasoning scores and cross-cultural adaptability assessments, constitute a multidimensional certification profile recognized by partner institutions, space agencies, and international research universities.

