## Part XV — The Martian Eco Graduate Profile

A Martian Eco graduate is not defined by occupation, affiliation, or the planet they inhabit.

They are defined by a demonstrated and institutionally certified capability architecture:

Scientific reasoning and cross-disciplinary systems modeling. Psychological resilience — measured, trained, and tested under conditions of graduated stress and genuine uncertainty. Ethical judgment capable of operating in domains without settled precedent. AI fluency combined with epistemic sovereignty — the ability to use intelligent systems powerfully while remaining cognitively independent of them. Ecological systems literacy applicable to both terrestrial and extraterrestrial environments. Cross-cultural adaptability and cooperative leadership under conditions of high diversity and high stakes. Long-horizon civilizational thinking across generational timescales.

This profile does not produce astronauts alone. It produces the lawyers who will draft interplanetary law. The engineers who will design closed-loop life support. The psychologists who will develop behavioral health protocols for deep space. The governors who will build institutions for settlements that do not yet exist. The teachers who will carry this framework forward. And the citizens — on Earth and beyond it — who will hold all of these people accountable.

They are not trained to serve a civilization.

They are prepared to build one, and to question what they build.

