## Closing Statement

Education has always been civilization's most consequential infrastructure. Not because it transmits culture — though it does — but because it decides, generation by generation, what kinds of human beings civilization produces.

What is being specified in this document is not a school. It is a civilizational training system for human behavioral adaptability under conditions of unprecedented novelty, complexity, and consequence.

The technology required for multiplanetary life is being engineered with extraordinary rigor and investment.

The question that remains is whether the human beings who will inhabit that future are being prepared with equivalent seriousness.

Martian Eco answers: they must be.

And here, in precise and testable architectural terms, is how.

