## Part VII — Facilitator Architecture

The MVP cannot function with conventional teachers. It requires a distinct professional profile: the Martian Eco Facilitator.

### Facilitator Profile

A Martian Eco Facilitator holds competency in at least two of the six pillars at research depth, certification in simulation facilitation and psychological safety protocols, training in cross-cultural collaborative facilitation, and demonstrated capacity for epistemic humility — the ability to model uncertainty, intellectual revision, and genuine inquiry rather than authoritative knowledge delivery.

### Certification Program

The MVP includes a parallel Facilitator Certification Program running six months before student cohort intake and continuing throughout the three years. Certification covers: simulation safety protocol methodology; Reality Anchoring Layer facilitation; cross-cultural collaborative design; longitudinal behavioral observation and PSUIS data collection; and the epistemic hierarchy architecture. Certified facilitators constitute the MVP's most important human infrastructure asset.

### Facilitator-to-Student Ratios

Track A standard curriculum: 1 facilitator per 20 students. Track A project phases: 1 facilitator per 10 students. Track B simulation exercises at Level 1-2: 1 facilitator per 8 students. Track B simulation exercises at Level 3 and above: 1 facilitator per 4 students, plus a certified psychological welfare monitor present at all times.

