## Closing Statement

The Martian Eco MVP is not the vision. It is the first honest encounter between the vision and reality.

Every assumption in the blueprint — about how young people respond to simulation-based stress training, about whether AI epistemic fluency can be developed through structured pedagogy, about whether a truly multicultural cohort can collaborate effectively across language and cultural difference on civilizational-scale problems — gets tested here, under real conditions, with real students, with real welfare at stake.

The question the MVP is ultimately asking is not whether Martian Eco is a beautiful idea.

It is whether it is a true one.

And truth, in this framework as in all others, is determined by what happens when you stop writing and start building.

